{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"05d48bfac04d8310268ab58668d8e1a29fa5887c356b179f0c9eec365370b273","packTokens":6671,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":6590,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff or admin user requests the Orders per Day report for a date range, the portal shall return one row per date with the number of orders and the order value.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 2 non-cancelled orders on 2026-03-02 with line totals 100.00 and 50.00, and 1 order on 2026-03-03 for 20.00 when staff calls GET /reports/orders-per-day?start=2026-03-02&end=2026-03-03 then The response status is 200 and the returned rows are (2026-03-02, 2, 150.00) and (2026-03-03, 1, 20.00)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff or admin user requests the Top Products report for a date range, the portal shall return one row per product with quantity sold and revenue, ordered by revenue descending.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product A sold 5 units at 10.00 and Product B sold 1 unit at 80.00 in the range when staff calls GET /reports/top-products for that range then The returned list is [(B, 1, 80.00), (A, 5, 50.00)]\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff or admin user requests the Revenue per Customer report for a date range, the portal shall return one row per customer with the number of orders and revenue.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Customer A has 2 orders totalling 300.00 and Customer B has 1 cancelled order in the range when staff calls GET /reports/revenue-per-customer for that range then The returned rows contain (A, 2, 300.00) and no row for Customer B\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a report is requested with a start date and end date, the portal shall include only orders whose submission date, in the business timezone, falls within the inclusive range.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given orders submitted on 2026-02-28, 2026-03-01 and 2026-03-31 and 2026-04-01 when staff requests Orders per Day with start=2026-03-01 and end=2026-03-31 then The returned rows cover only 2026-03-01 and 2026-03-31\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a customer user requests any report or report export, then the portal shall reject the request with status 403.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a signed-in customer user when they call GET /reports/top-products and GET /reports/top-products.csv then Both response statuses are 403 and no report data is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a staff or admin user exports a report, the portal shall return a UTF-8 comma-separated CSV file with a header row, the on-screen columns in on-screen order, ISO 8601 dates and '.' as decimal separator.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given the Orders per Day report for a range has rows (2026-03-02, 2, 150.00) when staff calls GET /reports/orders-per-day.csv for that range then The response file's first line is the header 'Date,Number of orders,Order value' and the next line is '2026-03-02,2,150.00'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When any of the listed business actions occurs (user invited or deactivated; product created, changed or retired; price or customer price list changed; order created, amended, confirmed, cancelled or status changed; invoice created or marked paid; ERP import succeeded or failed), the portal shall write an audit record with event type, actor, target record and timestamp.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a staff user confirms order 42 when the confirm call returns 200 then An audit row exists with event 'Order confirmed', the staff user as actor, order 42 as target and a timestamp\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a non-admin user requests audit history, then the portal shall reject the request with status 403.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a staff user and an admin user when each calls GET /admin/audit-logs then The staff response status is 403 and the admin response status is 200 with a list of audit records\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall retain order, invoice and audit records for at least 7 years and shall deactivate rather than delete users so their links to orders and invoices remain.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a customer user who placed order 42 when an admin deactivates the user then The user record's status field is Deactivated, order 42 and its invoice are still returned to other users of that customer, and the user's sign-in returns an error\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user is invited, a password reset is requested, or an order is confirmed, amended, out for delivery, cancelled or rejected, the portal shall send the matching template email through the configured email provider.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a stubbed email provider and order 42 in status Picking when staff sets order 42 to Out for Delivery then One email with the 'Order out for delivery' template referencing order 42 is sent to the ordering user's address at the provider stub\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If sending a notification email fails, then the portal shall still complete the triggering action and record the failed email with its error.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given the email provider stub returns an error when staff confirms order 42 then The response status is 200, order 42's status field is Confirmed, and an email notification row has status Failed with the error message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the scheduled stock import runs (default 02:00, configurable), the portal shall read the ERP CSV from the configured location and set stock quantity for each valid row's product, leaving products not in the file unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given products P1 (stock 5) and P2 (stock 9), and a file containing only 'P1,12' when the stock import job runs then P1's stock record value is 12 and P2's stock record value is still 9\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the stock import validates a file, the portal shall reject the whole file if it is empty or missing required headers, and otherwise apply valid rows and reject rows with unknown or duplicate product codes or non-numeric or negative quantities, recording received, processed and rejected counts with error details.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a file with 4 rows: one valid, one unknown code, one quantity 'abc', one quantity -3 when the stock import job runs then The import record shows received 4, processed 1, rejected 3 with one error detail per rejected row\",\n    \"Given a file with no header row when the stock import job runs then The import record status is Failed and no stock value changes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall not send any stock or inventory write request to the ERP.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an ERP endpoint stub that records requests when the stock import job runs and an order is submitted and delivered then The stub's recorded request count is 0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a stock import finishes, the portal shall show its status and counts on the System/Import status screen and write an 'ERP import succeeded' or 'ERP import failed' audit record.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a stock import that failed on missing headers when an admin calls GET /admin/imports then The returned latest import has status Failed with its error message, and an audit row 'ERP import failed' exists\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a customer user requests an order, invoice, address, price, user or account record belonging to another customer, then the portal shall return status 404 without the record's data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a buyer of Customer A and order 77 belonging to Customer B when the buyer calls GET /orders/77 and GET /invoices/{B's invoice id} then Both response statuses are 404 and the responses contain no Customer B data\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer user lists orders or invoices, the portal shall return all records of that user's customer company and no others.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given users U1 and U2 of Customer A each placed one order and Customer B has one order when U1 calls GET /orders then The returned list contains exactly U1's and U2's orders\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a user calls an endpoint outside their role (customer calling staff or admin endpoints, staff calling admin endpoints, or an unauthenticated caller), then the portal shall reject the request server-side with status 401 for unauthenticated and 403 otherwise.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an unauthenticated client, a customer user and a staff user when each calls POST /admin/products then The response statuses are 401, 403 and 403 respectively\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If sign-in fails for any reason, then the portal shall return the same generic invalid-credentials error message without revealing whether the email exists.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a known email with wrong password and an unknown email when each is submitted to POST /auth/sign-in then Both response statuses are 401 with an identical error message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a password-reset link older than its configured lifetime (default 1 hour) or an invitation older than its configured lifetime (default 7 days) is used, then the portal shall reject it with an expired-link error.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a reset token issued 61 minutes ago when it is submitted to POST /auth/reset-password then The response status is 400 with error code 'link_expired' and the password is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an unexpected server error occurs, then the portal shall return a generic error message with a reference id and no stack trace or internal details.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given the database is made unavailable when a client calls GET /orders then The response status is 500 and the body contains a message and reference id but no stack trace, SQL or file paths\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an order status change is requested other than Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for Delivery→Delivered or a permitted cancellation, then the portal shall reject it with status 409.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given order 42 in status Received when staff requests status Picking then The response status is 409 and order 42's status field is still Received\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer cancels an order, the portal shall set it to Cancelled only if its status is Received and otherwise reject the cancellation with status 409.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given order 1 in Received and order 2 in Confirmed when the customer calls POST /orders/{id}/cancel for each then Order 1 response is 200 with status Cancelled; order 2 response is 409 and its status stays Confirmed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff reject or cancel an order, the portal shall set it to Cancelled only if its status is Received or Confirmed and otherwise reject with status 409.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given order 1 in Confirmed and order 2 in Picking when staff calls POST /staff/orders/{id}/reject for each then Order 1 status field is Cancelled; order 2 response status is 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff save an order as Delivered, the portal shall create a linked Unpaid invoice in the same transaction so that either both are saved or neither is.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given order 42 in Out for Delivery when staff sets it to Delivered then Order 42 status is Delivered and one invoice row linked to order 42 has status Unpaid\",\n    \"Given invoice creation is forced to fail when staff sets order 42 to Delivered then The response is an error, order 42 status field is still Out for Delivery and no invoice row exists\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the daily overdue job runs, the portal shall mark Overdue every Unpaid invoice whose invoice date plus the system-wide payment term (default 30 days) has passed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given payment term 30 days, Unpaid invoices dated 31 and 29 days ago, and a Paid invoice dated 40 days ago when the overdue job runs then Only the 31-day invoice record's status is Overdue; the others are unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice paid, the portal shall record status Paid, the payment date and the staff user, and shall reject any status change of a Paid invoice with status 409.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an Overdue invoice when staff calls POST /staff/invoices/{id}/mark-paid with date 2026-03-10 then The invoice record has status Paid, payment date 2026-03-10 and the staff user; a second mark-paid call returns status 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorised user downloads an invoice PDF, the portal shall return a PDF rendered from the stored invoice record showing tax-exclusive line prices and no tax lines.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoice 9 of Customer A with 2 lines when a Customer A user calls GET /invoices/9/pdf then The response status is 200, content type is application/pdf and the file text contains the invoice number and both line totals\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer submits an order, the portal shall set the earliest delivery date to the next working day if submitted on a working day before the configured cut-off (default 14:00 business time), and otherwise to the second working day, where working days are Monday–Friday excluding configured public holidays.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no holidays configured when the delivery-date calculation is called for Tue 13:59, Tue 14:00 and Sat 10:00 then The returned dates are Wed, Thu and Tue respectively\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer views a product or places an order, the portal shall use the price from the customer's assigned price list and shall keep the placed order's line prices unchanged after later price-list changes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Customer A on Price List A with Product X at 10.00 and an order placed at 10.00 when Price List A changes X to 12.00 and the customer calls GET /products/X and GET /orders/{id} then The product response price is 12.00 and the order line price value is 10.00\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer submits an order with a quantity above the imported stock, the portal shall accept the order in status Received.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product X with stock 2 when the customer submits an order for 5 of X then The response status is 201 and the order record has status Received with quantity 5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a basket that has already been turned into an order is submitted again, then the portal shall reject the submission with status 409 without creating another order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a basket just submitted as order 42 when the same basket submit request is sent again then The response status is 409 and the customer's order count is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a customer repeats an order or loads a saved basket template, the portal shall add the items at current price-list prices, skip retired products and return a notice listing skipped products.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a previous order with products X (now 12.00) and Y (retired) when the customer calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat then The returned basket contains X at 12.00 and not Y, and the response notice field lists Y\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If staff edit an order whose status is not Received, then the portal shall reject the edit with status 409.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given order 1 in Received and order 2 in Confirmed when staff change a line quantity on each then Order 1 response is 200 with the new quantity; order 2 response status is 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an uploaded file is not an image or PDF or exceeds 10 MB, then the portal shall reject the upload with status 400.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an admin user when they upload an 11 MB JPEG and a 1 MB .exe as product images then Both response statuses are 400 with a validation error message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall provide the listed customer, staff and admin screens, each usable at 360 px viewport width as well as tablet and desktop widths in the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given each listed screen opened at 360 px, 768 px and 1280 px widths when a tester completes the screen's main task then The task completes with no horizontal scrolling or clipped controls\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a list or search has no results, the portal shall display an empty-state message specific to that list (search results, basket, orders, invoices, templates, products, report results).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a customer with no orders and an empty basket when a tester opens My orders and Basket then Each screen shows its empty-state message instead of a blank list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While a catalogue, search, basket, checkout, order submission, invoice download, report or staff queue request is in progress, the portal shall display a loading indicator and keep the order submit button disabled until the submission completes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given network throttled to slow 3G when a tester submits an order then A loading indicator is shown and the submit button cannot be pressed again until the confirmation screen appears\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall be deployable through the build pipeline to separate staging and production environments in one cloud region of the client's account, serving production only over HTTPS.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a merged change when the pipeline runs and a tester requests the production URL over http then The change is deployed to staging then production, and the http request is redirected to https\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history and staff order queue respond quickly at expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day).\",\n  \"Main customer and staff flows meet WCAG 2.1 AA.\",\n  \"Order, invoice and audit data retention.\",\n  \"Passwords stored hashed.\",\n  \"Reports reflect current data.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}